@startuml seq-10-fee-replacement
!include style.iuml
title Fee replacement: a new version of the same nonce, committed before it is broadcast\npayment: Sent · bump → Sent, Sent · cancel_replace → Sent (C2, C6, C7, C11, C13, C21; H-124, H-175, H-199; nonce-and-crash spike sections 6 and 7)
autonumber "<b>0."

actor Owner
participant "Web app" as Web
database "Store" as Store
participant "Wallet lane" as Lane
participant "Signer" as Signer
participant "RPC / Base" as Chain
participant "Receipt follower" as Follower

note over Store : payment I is Sent: version v1 {nonce n, maxFee f1, tip p1, raw1, hash1}
loop no receipt for any stored version
  Follower -> Chain : eth_getTransactionReceipt(hash1)
  Chain --> Follower : null
end
alt no receipt after k polls, or maxFee f1 below the current base fee
  Lane -> Chain : base fee, priority fee; GasPriceOracle getL1FeeUpperBound
  Lane -> Lane : f2 = max(1.125 × f1, current), p2 = max(1.125 × p1, current)\n(+12.5% covers geth's 10% PriceBump and reth)
  alt f2 within the fee reserve held for I (C11)
    Lane -> Signer : sign the same transfer, nonce n, fees (f2, p2)
    Signer --> Lane : raw2
    Lane -> Store : commit and sync: append version v2 {raw2, hash2 = keccak256(raw2)}
    note right of Store
      before any broadcast of raw2 (C6), synced to disk (C21): a kill or a power loss
      here leaves v2 stored or never sent; PaymentLane_bug_C21bump finds a double
      payment when this sync is left out
    end note
    Lane -> Chain : eth_sendRawTransaction(raw2), then raw1 (every version, newest first)
    Chain --> Lane : v2 accepted; raw1: "replacement transaction underpriced" (expected)
  else the reserve would be exceeded
    Lane -> Store : stop bumping; keep rebroadcasting; tell the owner the fee is above the reserve
  end
end
Follower -> Chain : receipts of v1 and v2
alt v2 mined
  Follower -> Store : I Included with v2; v1 marked replaced
else v1 mined before it was evicted
  Follower -> Store : I Included with v1; v2 marked replaced
end
note right of Store : any version's receipt settles the payment (C6); row: Sent · receipt [blk == 'own'] → Included

== The owner cancels a sent payment ==
Owner -> Web : Cancel this payment
Web -> Store : command into the lane {payment I, cancel, version} (C2)
Lane -> Signer : sign a zero-value transfer to the wallet itself at nonce n, fee above every stored version
Signer --> Lane : raw3
Lane -> Store : commit and sync: append version v3 {kind cancel} (owner-authorized, C21)
note right of Store : row: Sent · cancel_replace → Sent (CancelReplace)
Lane -> Chain : broadcast v3, v2, v1
alt v3 mined
  Follower -> Store : I Included with the cancel version
  note right of Store : row: Sent · receipt [blk == 'own' or blk == 'own_cancel'] → Included
  Follower -> Store : at finalized: I Cancelled, "not paid" (its fee was spent)
  note right of Store : row: Included · finality [blk_fin and blk == 'own_cancel'] → Cancelled (Settle)
else v1 or v2 mined first
  Follower -> Store : I Included, then Confirmed at finalized: "paid; the cancel came too late" (H-177)
  note right of Store : row: Included · finality [blk_fin and blk != 'own_cancel' and blk_ok] → Confirmed
end
note over Owner, Follower
  Past the burn point a cancel can only race; it never reports "did not run" (C13, H-199):
  payment Sent · cancel_or_switch_off → Sent. A mined cancel is never Confirmed, and a mined
  paying version never Cancelled (PaymentLane ReportedIsTrue; races.feature).
end note

== A foreign transaction takes nonce n (the exported key used elsewhere) ==
Follower -> Chain : nonce n consumed, no stored hash has a receipt
Follower -> Store : wait until that block is finalized (about 20 min; R-4)
note right of Store : Sent · receipt [blk == 'foreign' and not blk_fin] → Sent
Follower -> Chain : fetch the foreign transaction; recover its signer;\nask a second, independent RPC for the finalized block (C7)
alt proven: signer == wallet, nonce == n, hash not stored, both RPCs agree
  Follower -> Store : I → Waiting with a card that says what happened
  note right of Store : Sent · receipt [blk == 'foreign' and blk_fin and verified] → Waiting
else one RPC's word only
  Follower -> Store : I stays Sent; the owner is told the RPCs disagree
  note right of Store : Sent · receipt [blk == 'foreign' and blk_fin and not verified] → Sent (LieForeign)
end
Owner -> Web : approves again
Web -> Store : Pay; I re-enters the lane and takes a new nonce at its start commit
@enduml
